== first-step logit fidelity vs DENSE (n=3 prompts, ctx=16384, preset=mid, quant=nf4) ==
             arm  top1 agree  KL(dense||arm)  dense-top1 rank  top5 overlap   blocks
      dense_true       3/3           0.00000             0.00          5.0/5        0
  dense_true/dec       3/3           0.00000             0.00          5.0/5        0
        baseline       3/3           0.00000             0.00          4.3/5      640
    baseline/dec       1/3           3.62980             6.00          1.0/5      640

Read every arm against BASELINE, not against dense: the
baseline gap is what compression already costs and is not the
feature's doing. An arm level with baseline has added nothing.

The */dec rows are the SECOND token, scored against the dense
control at that SAME position. dense_true/dec is the self-check:
it has no compression in it anywhere, so it must read ~0. If it
does not, the positions are misaligned and no row here means
anything -- which is exactly how this harness reported KL 10.579
for a defect that did not exist.
